WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.400
Huh?

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.980
What a pain.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.360
What's wrong?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.360
My mom asked me to pick up
some soy sauce on my way home.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.360
Jeez.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.610
She should get my little brother to do it instead.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.490
Now, now...

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.740
Natsuki, that just means she depends on you.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.000
Hmph.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.500
Natsuki...

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.540
You have a little brother?!

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.100
Huh?

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.730
I never mentioned it?

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.980
This is <i>so</i> the first I've heard of it!

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.770
When was that written into your backstory?

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.320
What do you mean, "when?"

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.780
This isn't some old school mecha anime.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.610
What's his name?

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.490
Oh? It's Lloyd.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.620
Lloyd?

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.370
That's an unusual name for a Japanese person.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.410
I don't think it's all that different from "Claire."

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.120
Older? Younger?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.500
Male? Female?

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.330
I told you, he's my <i>little brother!</i>

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.420
Oh, yeah.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.340
He's two years younger than me.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.090
Well? What school does he go to?

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.380
Does he look like you?

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.590
What are his hobbies and talents?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.140
Height? Weight?

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.760
What does he wash first in the bath?

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.220
What does he usually talk about?

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.100
What school activities was he into,
and what did he learn from them?

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.190
What's his personal motto?

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.600
Now, what question are we on?

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.230
You guys are getting too into this!

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.480
But isn't that natural?

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.820
Because if he's Natsuki's little brother, that means...

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.240
he's basically <i>our</i> little brother, too!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.240
I get it!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.080
Um, wrong...

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.950
What kind of logic warped you to that conclusion?

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.460
A martial artist's path is long and treacherous.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.340
Is Lloyd prepared to walk that path?

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.380
Most likely not!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.170
And why are you nominating him as your successor?!

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.340
Also, what was that question about earlier?!

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.430
What does he wash first in the bath?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.600
How would I know the answer to that?!

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.140
O-Oh, I guess...

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:35.400
Just because you're siblings, you don't
necessarily take baths together.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.030
W-Well, we did take them
together when we were little...

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.280
Take this, Lloyd!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.910
Cut it out!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.740
You're so annoying!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.500
It's normal to do that kind of thing when you're little!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.870
<i>This</i> is the problem with only children!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.000
Really?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.170
Sorry.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.670
Anyway, you guys don't know anything
about the reality of having a little brother.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.260
In that case,

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.470
why don't we all go to Natsuki's house to hang out,

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.550
so we can experience the reality together?

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.180
Good idea.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.230
I should see him with my own eyes and ascertain whether

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.100
he has what it takes to be my successor.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.480
I can't wait!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.940
What?!

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.900
Take me with you.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.740
What a pain this has turned into.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.840
Wandering minstrel seal.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.850
Today, I think we should sell poems on the street!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.680
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.140
Questions will not be answered!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:56.150
But don't you need a license or
something to be a street vendor?

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.100
Really?

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.900
But those people who sell accessories
and things on the street are obviously...

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.820
Why are you basing your judgment on them?

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.360
It should be fine if we set up near the station.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.030
What?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.160
Because that land belongs to my family!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.040
The area around the station...

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.580
...is your personal...

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.620
...property?!

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.420
Why did you divide up the line?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.510
Well, have you already written the
poems we'll be selling by the station?

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.630
Perish the thought!

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.930
We're all going to write them now, of course.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.180
How disorganized is this plan?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.640
We'll take the poems of girls still in high school...

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.690
hot and steamy off the press...

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.940
and sell them outside!

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.440
Why did you make it sound so obscene?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.230
But even if you ask us to write poems out of the blue...

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.240
No need to think so hard about it.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.660
You don't have to worry about

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.040
saying something insightful or
getting to the heart of anything.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:57.830
Yesterday, I saw a person selling poems
on the street, so I bought some...

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.580
And it was just random junk
written in sloppy handwriting

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.210
to create the atmosphere of poetry.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.840
Don't say any more.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.210
We'll get complaints.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.590
That sounds easy!

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.550
That sounds like something even we can do.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.970
For something like this,

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.180
the bad handwriting seems to be the crucial point.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.060
That's exactly right, Natsuki!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.230
No matter what you write,

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.520
it looks like words of wisdom if it's in bad handwriting!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.150
This is the absolutely crucial point!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.770
R-Right...

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.230
Just keep that point in mind,

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:28.610
then randomly select phrases like
"Thank you" and write them down,

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.070
and you're done!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.740
Let's get writing!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.200
Phrases like "Thank you"?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.580
I'm done.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.000
That was fast, Botan.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.040
This is what you meant by
phrases like "Thank you," right?

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.460
That's just extortion!

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.970
That's violating Article 249 of the Japanese Criminal Code!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.140
I thought I was on the right track...

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.430
I'm finished, too.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.970
Oh? Let me see!

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.890
I'm quite confident in this one.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.150
There's no escape!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:04.570
Why are you all making poems on
society's negative qualities?

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.730
Let's try to get away from the word "thank," shall we?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.190
Well then, does this work?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.410
"Think Tank U..." "Thank U..." "Thank You..."

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.240
Oh, I get it!

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.250
Karin, you're amazing!

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.710
That's all wrong!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.920
You've all got completely the wrong idea!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:27.670
This is what I mean by phrases like "Thank you"!

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.380
That seems wrong, too.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.050
I don't know how to react to that.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.350
It's okay to fail sometimes!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.100
It's partially my fault for being so
disappointed by your stupidity.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.270
So now...

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.900
We'll change the keyword to
"phrases that warm the heart!"

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.270
Of course.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.610
Heartwarming, huh?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.030
Why did you rephrase that in English?

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.910
I will write an example.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.330
Wrong from the get-go?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.330
That only warms the body.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.080
But the heated table is like the
heart of the Japanese people, right?

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.750
That's true. It's the Japanese Heart.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.340
Again, why the English rewording?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.090
I'm certain that mine will be heartwarming.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.850
Uh, that doesn't quite reach the heart...

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.190
That's true.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:27.440
When you touch a sheep, it's actually kinda greasy.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.440
That's not why it's wrong!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.530
Since it's come to this...

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:33.610
I <i>know</i> this will shine a ray of sunlight into your heart!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.450
Here!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.120
That only warms the nasty part of the heart.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.000
Really? I don't think that's true...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.370
What about you, Natsuki?

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.300
I couldn't think of anything.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.510
You made fun of my heated table and
then you did exactly the same thing?!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.760
Sorry I kept you all waiting!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.140
What's up, Karin?

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.390
The thing that warms my heart is...

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:02.890
This!

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:05.940
That does make me happy!

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.520
That's definitely a heartwarming
moment in anyone's life!

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.270
We finally found the right answer!

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.280
Well,

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.030
what do we do with these?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.610
I'm pretty sure we can't sell them...

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.790
I'm a seal, after all!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.920
There!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.250
Wow, they fly really well.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.170
I'm throwing the next one!

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.550
Karin, do your best.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.420
Okay, okay, I'm after her!

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.590
No fair! You just threw one.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.890
I'm the one who got us the sign boards!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.640
Now, now, you two.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:42.850
Here I go!

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.940
How did things turn out like this?

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.410
Hello!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.740
They really came...

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.330
We told you we'd all come over.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.920
Yeah, but there was another "Record" in between,

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.710
so I figured maybe you'd forgotten—

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.960
Yay! Love and peace!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.300
Your enthusiasm is annoying!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.300
We're coming in!

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:19.800
Wow!

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:20.220
Natsuki's house!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.140
Yay! Yahoo!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:24.560
Peace! Peace! Double peace!

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.310
The approximately one of you
who's being annoying can <i>beat it</i>.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.480
Anyway, let's go up to my room.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.860
No way.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.530
First, we want to see the little dude. Your brother!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.410
Oh. That's right.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.660
Lloyd! Come here! You've got two seconds!

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.410
Two seconds?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.540
What is it, Sis?

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.790
He really came!

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.460
Then, let me formally introduce him.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.340
This is my little brother, Lloyd.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.380
Why are you treating me like an object?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.920
Never mind! Just be quiet!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.010
It'll be over soon.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:10:59.930
Tch.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.010
So this is Natsuki's little brother?

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.060
She's laughing at me!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.520
I don't know how to react to that!

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.690
Why is my own sister laughing, too?!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.820
It's so annoying how you humor everyone else!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.990
Lloyd, you mustn't use that tone.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.490
You should call her "my dear sister, Natsuki," as is proper.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.580
Like hell! What kinda snob are you?!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:32.920
Lloyd!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.540
You think you can talk like that just
because you're in middle school?!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.670
How dare you speak like that to your upperclassman?!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.680
Are you in any place to say that?!

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:44.050
Overwashed seal.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.810
So this is Natsuki's room!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.100
Don't stare at it like that.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.860
I didn't have time to clean u—

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.190
What? That was fast!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.400
You really are a pain.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.700
It smells like Natsuki!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.450
I give up! I give up! I give up!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:06.070
Natsuki, that's... an impressive
execution of the Boston crab.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.910
I give up! I give up! I give up! I give up!

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.080
Where did you learn it?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:09.370
Oh, well, as you know, I have a little brother.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.460
I give up! I give up! I give up! I give up!

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.330
Oh!

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.170
So having a little brother makes you good at the Boston crab.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.420
Karin, I don't think you
should watch any more of this.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.380
I already said I give up!

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.180
Oh, sorry.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.140
I was just doing like I always do...

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.180
and I put you in a lock.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.930
I feel sorry for your little brother!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:34.140
When Lloyd turns twenty, I'm taking him out drinking!

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.900
Welcome!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.400
How have things been lately?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.150
Well... okay, I guess.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.190
I see.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.780
We'll eat wasabi octopus and have
a heart-to-heart talk till dawn!

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:50.200
I see your image of bars is still
centered around wasabi octopus.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.580
Hey!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.710
Natsuki, you've got a teddy bear sleeping in your bed!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.340
Oh, darn.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.750
Th-That's, um...

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.630
I just left it lying around!

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.590
Oh? But it was even tucked in!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.760
Stop it!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.350
I beg you! Please, stop!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:11.390
What?

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.100
But it isn't strange at all.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.520
I love stuffed animals, too.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.810
R-Really?

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:19.610
Hey, Natsuki, what's his name?

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.610
It's Chucky.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:25.280
So it does... have a name.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.860
Dammit!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.570
You jerks!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.490
Just go home!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:33.080
Come on. We're sorry, Natsuki.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.790
By the way, we brought...

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.580
sleepover kits with us!

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:40.840
Go home!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.430
I really screwed up.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.060
I can't believe all this happened because

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.190
I let it slip that I have a little brother.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.360
Sis?

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.570
What is it, Lloyd?

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.610
How long do you plan on staying in there?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.360
Some of us are still waiting for a turn.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.240
Just 7 minutes and 21 seconds longer.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.570
Okay.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:21.330
I should at least have hidden Chucky.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.340
Lloyd! The bath's free!

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.050
Oh, thanks!

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.020
Oh, looking good.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.980
Now, I'll move that over here...

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.480
What a good little boy you are, Chucky.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.110
It's almost time for beddy-byes!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.190
Welcome back, Natsuki!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.650
Chucky just got out of the bath, too.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.570
Natsuki, where's the next issue of this manga?

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.280
Sorry, the batteries in your game are about to run out.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.660
You're all making yourselves way too comfortable here.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.260
There's something I've been
wondering about for a while...

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.720
About what?

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.260
Natsuki, which one is the "main body"?

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.140
Huh?

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.220
You know, is it this...

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.520
Or this?

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.560
What do you mean by the "main body"?!

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.520
Why would <i>this</i> be my main body?!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.810
But it does move from time to time.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:26.820
Almost like it has a life of its own.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.650
It does not!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.490
Sometimes it sways in the wind, but that's all.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:35.990
It also wags like a dog's tail when you're happy!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.370
It does not!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.200
Huh?

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.410
It looked like it moved just now...

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:44.130
Maybe my eyes are tired from looking
at a computer screen for too long...

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.880
Charging...

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.750
Well, setting that aside,

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.460
what I'm wondering about is...

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.380
If that thing is actually the main body...

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:57.310
then, what is the humanoid part
attached to the bottom of it?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.060
I can't really answer that.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.060
I've been wondering about that too, to be honest.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:06.400
Sometimes I've found myself talking to it instead of you.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.110
What?!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.230
That's so embarrassing!

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:11.990
And here I thought you were talking to me!

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.280
Wait, why the hell?!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.700
She went along with it before objecting.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.780
She's never done that before.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.120
We should mark it on the
calendar as our own holiday.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:23.080
So, what is the part attached to the bottom, anyway?

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.080
It should be obvious if you think about it!

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.250
Thinking about it...

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.250
maybe it's an interpreter?

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.920
Hair treatment is very important.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.340
You think I'm just its servant?!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.970
Thinking about it...

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:40.470
Maybe it's like one of those clear character
files that you get in manga magazines.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.810
You're saying I'm just a nice bonus?!

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:47.650
Thinking about it, it's like that
stuff they put on salisbury steaks...

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.280
You're saying I'm parsley, the
most useless thing on the plate?!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:55.160
Thinking about it, it's like those sacs
attached to a salmon fry's stomach...

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.990
You're saying I'll eventually
be absorbed and disappear?!

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.870
Thinking about it, it's like the
nose bladder on a hooded seal...

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:08.000
You're saying I'm an organ used
for frightening predators?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.630
More importantly, you don't have
to reference things from Episode 1.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:16.180
Come on! Stop picking on me already.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.430
I'm sensitive about my cowlick.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.100
It's a cowlick?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.100
It's gone way past that!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.610
So this hair is actually a cowlick?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:33.360
It has such a beautiful wave to it,
I assumed you permed it like that.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.860
It's not beautiful at all.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.820
If you're that self-conscious about it,

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.820
I could straighten it for you.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.120
No way!

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:42.910
Why not?

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.000
Because I know...

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.710
it'll just turn out like this.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.010
H-How is that possible?!

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.880
Then, why don't we just cut it off?

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:01.140
Sewing scissors!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.850
I thought something like this might happen,

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:06.680
so I brought the sewing scissors
I inherited from my grandmother!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.770
So those actually exist...

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.230
Okay, fine.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.480
Try cutting it off.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:13.270
Sure.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.240
Y-You can't, Sakura!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.280
If you do, Natsuki's contents will fall out!

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:20.570
"Contents"?

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:21.240
Yes.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.030
Because, you know...

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.580
So, Natsuki will also...

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.290
Don't compare me to a flan cup!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:35.050
Though, come to think of it,
I tried cutting it off once before.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:36.710
What happened?

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:51.980
A second and a third one just sprang up in its place.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.020
I think doing it again would just encourage it.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.150
It's starting to sound like a curse.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.990
Did one of your ancestors mistreat
a clothes hanger or something?

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.280
There.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.200
But I like it.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:09.790
Natsuki's "thing."

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.750
After all, it's a part of Natsuki's whole.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.800
And that's the Natsuki I love.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.180
Sakura...

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.180
This is part of what makes you Natsuki.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.610
Actually, if you lost it, I wouldn't
think of you as Natsuki anymore!

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:35.900
Is this Natsuki?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.690
Or is Natsuki this?

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.190
Maybe without it—

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.360
I was an idiot to let myself get sentimental.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.570
There, there.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.910
But you're right. I can't imagine Natsuki without it.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:53.920
Maybe we should use image editing
software to erase it from a picture of her!

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.590
That sounds fun!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.130
Um... when did you take all of these?

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.340
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.800
Just a second.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.720
First, we open a random picture...

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.640
Once it's open in the image editing program,

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.350
select the area around it...

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.810
Then, I just have to click "delete."

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.700
What? What's going on here?

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.580
The whole room went dark!

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:57.250
That was a real shock.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:58.750
There was an unforeseen error,

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:00.710
and it even changed the ending...

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:02.050
What are you talking about?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.130
Oh, no.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.090
It's nothing.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:11.680
What's wrong?

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.970
Natsuki, you...

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:15.730
Yes?

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:22.110
Everyone, Natsuki's—

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:25.860
What is it, Claire?

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:27.530
You don't look well.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:29.780
More importantly, have you fixed the computer?

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.120
I want to continue with what we were doing before.

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:34.040
I want to see it, too!

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:35.330
Yeah, I can't wait to see it!

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:36.660
You said it!

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:48.800
A babirusa's tusks bend backwards as they grow,

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:51.680
until they look like they might even impale its own head!

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:54.260
I wonder if Natsuki's "thing" will do that, too.
